[{"id":"VRCE-7-8-1","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":8,"verse":1,"english":"On that host being sore pressed at its back by Padmanabha,* Mālyavăn turned back even as the ocean does on meeting with its shore. *Lit. the lotus-naveled-a name of Visnu.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.839,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-8-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7008001","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8be9d50f77fa076392c6030b5dc0d926b8c6aed05d3a484967ccc7a37faa80ef","compact":"5c2a833702bdaf792fc1ad2b0f9a00ebd3801fe07a07e77d26e94abe1a4aab2e","nasal":"5c2a833702bdaf792fc1ad2b0f9a00ebd3801fe07a07e77d26e94abe1a4aab2e"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-8-2","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":8,"verse":2,"english":"And with his eyes reddened, that night-ranger waxing wroth, shaking his head, addressed that prime of male persons Padmanabha, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.537,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-8-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7008002","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4bb10d50b0051f5893134030f1f042a2960e500e498988e2556063a2e9baddfc","compact":"034c55775f3d559af643beaeba7543801a025e0c9064c0241797b4baed7f0c21","nasal":"034c55775f3d559af643beaeba7543801a025e0c9064c0241797b4baed7f0c21"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-8-3","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":8,"verse":3,"english":"O Nārāyaṇa, you are ignorant of the timehonoured morality of Kşatriyas; and therefore like a base wight you slay us, desisting from fight and exercised with fear.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.458,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-8-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7008003","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4eae54a6ef4a9df902562b5a0ef1ba22f470f3d9fc8bb6e1776c02909d3077d1","compact":"9662921b5e86ad42da4fb59c02abd85be5513413096733f92d62cf7f43409f1e","nasal":"9662921b5e86ad42da4fb59c02abd85be5513413096733f92d62cf7f43409f1e"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-8-4","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":8,"verse":4,"english":"O lord of the celestials, he that commits the crime of slaying one that desists from fight cannot go to the celestial regions as the fruit of meritorious acts.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.86,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-8-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7008004","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"357813cf24a48aadc4da19cb551f1afa2892031f17d32f70f620295516434c51","compact":"926c9327ecf27bb74375be425d2850ae3edb33a81e85362145c078902b50f316","nasal":"bfae1aec3e1088632eea3b3de1715cac1e1ed5c32aa0b4dd9fc9bfa01d419f1d"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-8-5","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":8,"verse":5,"english":"If you are bent upon battle, a holder of the conch, the discus and the mace, taking up my post (here), I shall see (your strength). Do you show (me) the same.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-8-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7008005","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6a19ce3d2b4fdc0ac62f1fcdf3ba361876f876e1ccc70118065c40a52508a961","compact":"163e6feac826805d7a995558a5dc047634ce310cc06bb1588225cc48a4aa7d5b","nasal":"fa1283b957b1e010c836ba52ffacab2c3fb6dba24a09b35977302e7c438d1901"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-8-6","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":8,"verse":6,"english":"Seeing Mālyavān resembling the mountain, Mālyavān, stay, the powerful younger brother of the sovereign of the celestials spoke to him. I have removed the fear of the deities, affrighted at you, by promising that I will make root and branch work with the Räkşasas; and that same promise I am now fulfilling.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.645,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-8-6","DUTT-7-8-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7008006","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"961ff9d45944d8eef39355a0568cf086fcb296c422ed5a40b4f80362fb88b4d8","compact":"a494a7400c720d87b499fde2d26332e9b96df6a13d035d3a8a3092d3b6209b78","nasal":"44df7895e7bc2cc9c7dbe1b55e74d0321836457ed870ac857c27519010a27168"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-8-7","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":8,"verse":7,"english":"I should always lay down my life for serving the celestials and you I will slay even if you should go to the nethermost regions.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-8-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7008007","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0f1f2a721a9430f1341bc5fb2ecd3690668bdc712f961f62d81e6fe754705cd8","compact":"3c50fb20a6a3238da9820011ea5c4a2475de1ae1a406701c6528e2119ae7c226","nasal":"3c50fb20a6a3238da9820011ea5c4a2475de1ae1a406701c6528e2119ae7c226"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-8-8","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":8,"verse":8,"english":"As that god of gods having eyes resembling the red lotuses was speaking thus, the lord of Rākşasas in high wrath pierced his breast with a dart.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.75,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-8-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7008008","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"89b54d5437e3c91b7d7fe83eb84e985278e39cfd7c3a4449aaa9de6e128420cd","compact":"6007cd8aa38420f2520d8f58ae2c7cf404ec76a6828ed8f1c4406b2d1f8bf57f","nasal":"bc43f14d720762bdfec5eb282cb83a1e71ac789327bd63ff0af5a1c7c5daa507"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-8-9","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":8,"verse":9,"english":"And hurled by the hand of Mālyavān, the dart resonant with bells, appeared graceful on Hari's breast like lightening embosomed in clouds.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.778,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-8-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7008009","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9f2ee9da3e85f5721b606aed40b3758985473d31aba54f962df44b00d6ebdcfd","compact":"e07f3453ee0218b4f81c4b62bd925299bbe25e8aa934335c8c915f79bd82527c","nasal":"4c2645ee7fee44448ef45b51704847d2d86fd349c585b5f565409cc63de44d3b"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-8-10","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":8,"verse":10,"english":"Thereat drawing out the same dart, that one dear to the Wielder of the Dart,* having eyes resembling red lotuses, aiming at Mālyāvan, hurled it at him. *A name of Kārtikeya, the celestial generallissimo.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-8-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7008010","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e48a9a007bd3b18b40887385f36a253817e864a8fbdedf2e016793d57cdd6f05","compact":"569e1a97e50836c809a08ba9b99fbff469b67cf59a67366724e98515884e683a","nasal":"4f90c5581084a695042fc683cb1a325994ebc9afd34e7457923019209ab48962"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-8-11","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":8,"verse":11,"english":"Thereat the dart discharged by the hand of Govinda like to the Dart discharged by the hand of Skanda, rushing towards the Rākṣasa like a meteor coursing towards the Anjana mountain, descended on the spacious chest of the lord of the Rākşasas decked with the weight of a chain, even as the thunder clap bursts at the summit of the mountain.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-8-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7008011","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishE