a javelin made of black iror girt with many a thorn, he furiously smote that deity on the chest.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.853,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-8-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7008014","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"880729bcc57875f724ac836c6c887e8c4a3b66c19f8168f64ff3229623125612","compact":"f8c9ff49b5014b2f4cc845daedce3022cf65c1d8bfb8409261298934127d4275","nasal":"4534ff42dcaaa7f524aa3d6a3caac5954fd397f7bb589508a175d2b85f452fee"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-8-15","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":8,"verse":15,"english":"And that night-ranger delighting in battle, dealing a box at Vāsavā's younger brother, moved away a distance measuring a bow's length.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-8-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7008015","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"73954309cff1fc6780e479b33b0e3a073986031d7bf5d89d94b65aa272a0a993","compact":"06bafa9f9bad936e5c37ad90615c373e5af961a6f0b0c511501db76a44a4229c","nasal":"b0bf3104573a9356b797cbf536e3fcf7411a2bc6790ffbf63831549c892a3c8c"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-8-16","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":8,"verse":16,"english":"And now there arose a mighty tumult in the sky of 'Excellent!' 'Excellent!' and having struck Visnu, the Raksasa also hit Garuda.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-8-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7008016","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"059381522fe6b2b61ce8b3361e7a8b79b5d1e256017e585e1b55169a248f1cf7","compact":"a2a1f3d1202d3ef9934435260279e383c67117aa6f43ea88864daf64e6f57ace","nasal":"497b8dbe2757f61415a7eedf0f5bdb6344653d6e4f11521ab0b77f85a58b6963"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-8-17","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":8,"verse":17,"english":"Thereat Vinata's son, growing engaged, drove the Rākşasas away with the wind of his wings, even as the lusty wind bloweth about sere leaves.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.742,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-8-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7008017","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c24bef5ccdcd1fb29ef09e84722f5b839d51bc9cc173cc8375954e40efea0f66","compact":"eea3e11dc101d4cddbda2ae89a3c00cdcc77efcd47d3b7ae5a022e01e2b0a8c7","nasal":"eea3e11dc101d4cddbda2ae89a3c00cdcc77efcd47d3b7ae5a022e01e2b0a8c7"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-8-18","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":8,"verse":18,"english":"Seeing his elder brother driven by the wind produced by the wings of that bird, Sumali along with his forces, made for Lankā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-8-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7008018","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"25068e5f8fe0a2c19a1d783c4dd25734c73e02328e90700ee36c8cc9b9a34d49","compact":"063969d5fb3bffd01734fa2f8d76ff729d05f371cfce9ef1b16f3da2cad0868b","nasal":"4aee1c1be16f66461278bf567e8e2fd714da3b1abf628c40f5c81a180ff1da8f"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-8-19","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":8,"verse":19,"english":"And pushed off by the violence of the wind of (Garuda's) wings, the Rākṣasa Mālyavān also, joined by his own forces, departed for Lankā, covered with shame.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-8-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7008019","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cf0c8ef5570bd828a9db21e93dfe5a76d95327a8fff6b62a6d9b3ca2300e387a","compact":"29535ce642793ecedeec18be17fac8a40f